{"description":"eka view execution reports empty board when only planned containers exist, hiding queued work. Projection is scoped to active container (none), so shows Planned(0) Todo(0) ... 0/0 (0%) even though 8 work items across 2 fully-ticketed planned containers exist. Information is available via eka view board and eka view containers (correctly show 3/3 and 5/5 planned) but not surfaced in execution view. Every planning-\u003eexecution handoff passes through this state (activation locks plan immutable, belongs to /eka-execute), so user/agent asks 'what is queued?' at exactly this moment and gets misleading empty signal.","acceptanceCriteria":"1. eka view execution when no active container but \u003e=1 planned container shows queued planned containers summary (name, plan, items/tickets, status=planned) + hint to use eka view board/containers or activate. 2. Does not break active-container board (when active exists, show active board as before + optional queued hint). 3. No confusion between 0 queued vs 0 active. Verified with 2 planned containers, and with 0 planned containers (shows no queued state)."}